---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy and cookies"
  description="How DiaryFolio uses browser storage and optional Google Analytics."
>
  <article class="article">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Site information</p>
      <h1>Privacy and cookies</h1>
      <p>How DiaryFolio uses browser storage and optional analytics.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="article-lead">
        DiaryFolio is a static technical archive. Optional Google Analytics is disabled until you explicitly accept it.
      </p>

      <h2>Necessary browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        The site stores your light or dark theme preference in your browser. If analytics is configured, it also stores
        your analytics choice for up to 180 days so the consent question does not appear on every visit. These preferences
        are not used to follow you across other websites.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        If you accept analytics, DiaryFolio loads Google Analytics to understand aggregate usage such as pages visited and
        general browser or device information. Google Analytics may create first-party cookies whose names begin with{' '}
        <code>_ga</code>. Advertising storage and personalisation remain denied by this site’s analytics consent setting.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you reject analytics, the Google Analytics script is not loaded and no analytics request is sent. Learn more in{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Change your choice</h2>
      <p>
        Use <strong>Cookie settings</strong> in the footer at any time. Withdrawing consent stops Analytics on subsequent
        page loads and removes accessible DiaryFolio cookies whose names begin with <code>_ga</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The analytics choice described here does not grant advertising consent. Advertising must remain disabled unless a
        separate, appropriate consent-management process is configured.
      </p>

      <p><small>Last updated: 19 August 2026.</small></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
